From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:27:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: i2c: dongwoon,dw9800k: add a default lens
 position

A camera module without autofocus in user space still needs its lens
somewhere useful while it streams: with no current through the coil the
lens rests at the far end of its travel, which is beyond infinity on
some modules. The module maker's camera stack starts at a known position
(the OnePlus Pad 4's rear module: 450 of 1023).

Add dongwoon,default-position for that position. The lens is held there
only while the image sensor that refers to the actuator through
lens-focus streams, so that the coil carries no current while the
camera is idle.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml          | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml
index 046c0a88bcef..2cf53c071563 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9800k.yaml
@@ -65,6 +65,16 @@ properties:
     maximum: 0x3f
     default: 0x20
 
+  dongwoon,default-position:
+    description:
+      Lens position, as the 10-bit output current code, that the camera
+      module needs while its image sensor streams and no other position has
+      been asked for, e.g. the module maker's start position for focusing.
+      The actuator then holds the lens only while the image sensor that
+      refers to it through lens-focus streams.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    maximum: 1023
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
@@ -87,5 +97,6 @@ examples:
             dongwoon,sac-mode = <4>;
             dongwoon,clock-presc = <0>;
             dongwoon,timing-control = <16>;
+            dongwoon,default-position = <450>;
         };
     };
